WEBVTT

00:00:08,880 --> 00:00:15,040
After over three years of basically no change, this person's cancer, the lump,

00:00:15,040 --> 00:00:21,440
and my breast has come to life, since losing all my weight the first year after diagnosis,

00:00:21,440 --> 00:00:28,080
it's been very easy to feel, and it's always felt the same, the lump and the breast,

00:00:28,080 --> 00:00:34,560
firm had rigid. Now however, it's got a small area that is hard as a rock,

00:00:34,640 --> 00:00:41,760
and it seems to be attaching to skin visibly. It's like it's going to burst through soon.

00:00:42,960 --> 00:00:49,280
Seems similar to the attachment that creates the inverted nipple. I'm so scared,

00:00:49,280 --> 00:00:55,840
I don't know what to make of it. If I go to the regular doctor, they will push hard for surgery,

00:00:56,800 --> 00:01:04,240
but there's no alternative doctor close by that I know of who would monitor it as a

00:01:04,560 --> 00:01:14,880
open wound if I try black sand. I would feel assured it was a positive response to the MMS

00:01:14,880 --> 00:01:21,840
protocol I've been doing this last month, except unfortunately I've also been failing at my diet a

00:01:21,840 --> 00:01:31,520
lot recently, so could be pushing a bad change. I just don't know. Still feel great physically,

00:01:31,520 --> 00:01:36,640
getting some new blood work and a Dutch test in about a month. Then we'll also get more

00:01:36,640 --> 00:01:42,480
information in the meantime. I'm scared, straight back into a strict diet, LOL.

00:01:44,080 --> 00:01:51,040
Do such changes in a lump always mean bad news. I've been looking online for a source of black

00:01:51,040 --> 00:02:00,750
sand, but I can't find one yet. Do you have any leads for this? Also a loss as to how a doctor

00:02:00,830 --> 00:02:08,990
might a doctor locally who can monitor the black sand. You're going to have a very difficult time

00:02:08,990 --> 00:02:14,910
finding a local doctor who's going to monitor a black sand, topical black sand protocol,

00:02:15,870 --> 00:02:28,540
simply because it's so infrequently done. But to answer some of these prior questions here,

00:02:29,500 --> 00:02:34,780
is doing black sand on a breast tumor? Always the right thing to do.

00:02:36,300 --> 00:02:49,900
My answer to that would be no. We've had multiple patients do a black sand protocol on their breast.

00:02:50,940 --> 00:02:56,220
Over the years, some had a good experience with it, some had a bad experience with it,

00:02:56,460 --> 00:03:04,380
or it was good for a period of time and then it just seemed to just make a mess of things. It's

00:03:04,380 --> 00:03:11,900
very difficult to manage. You're always cleaning it. It seems like it's always coming out. It seems

00:03:12,940 --> 00:03:22,860
often it seems never ending, which is different than doing black sand on a topical melanoma.

00:03:23,420 --> 00:03:33,340
There's always an end point with melanoma. Though I've had people do it multiple, multiple times on

00:03:33,340 --> 00:03:42,060
that same spot still pulling the cancer out. There always was an end point and it always in my experience

00:03:42,060 --> 00:03:51,340
ended well. With breast cancer, it's a little bit different. It's just different in many different ways.

00:03:52,300 --> 00:03:59,100
I don't know that black sand is the right thing to do for that reason. Secondly, black sand is not

00:03:59,100 --> 00:04:08,940
going to have an effect on a cancer that is several millimeters below the surface. If the cancer

00:04:08,940 --> 00:04:16,460
breaks through the skin wall and you do have an open wound, then a person theoretically could use

00:04:16,460 --> 00:04:23,020
topical things on it. His blacks have the thing to go to right away. Well, for reasons I already

00:04:23,020 --> 00:04:27,980
stated, it may not be. So you've got to think long and hard before you're going to do that.

00:04:29,900 --> 00:04:35,100
The other negative black sand black sand could be very painful. Some people have done it on their

00:04:35,100 --> 00:04:42,140
breast or on a melanoma and it had not had any pain, but it does open up the wound more and it will draw.

00:04:42,540 --> 00:04:52,300
So there's pros and cons to doing it. So don't take that, don't take, don't make your decision thinking

00:04:52,300 --> 00:05:00,220
that that's going to be for sure the answer and I want to find somebody to do black sand.

00:05:00,940 --> 00:05:09,900
So that being said, on their topical things, a person could do if the cancer is near the surface,

00:05:10,780 --> 00:05:19,980
prior to a cancer breaking through the tissue from an alternative perspective. And then last

00:05:19,980 --> 00:05:29,500
comment on this is that I would caution anybody that is in this situation, just this person who wrote

00:05:29,580 --> 00:05:39,980
this is to not, you know, I'd question, you know, why are you completely against doing anything,

00:05:39,980 --> 00:05:45,900
standards of care wise. Of course, standards of care in this situation, depending on how big the

00:05:45,900 --> 00:05:53,980
masses there's all sorts of dependings there, I would want to do a mastectomy. Now, I know there's

00:05:53,980 --> 00:05:58,620
a lot of women that are completely 100% against doing mastectomy, but we've had people that have

00:05:59,500 --> 00:06:08,380
been that way and have done black sand and fought it for months to years and then finally succumbed

00:06:08,380 --> 00:06:17,420
to doing a mastectomy. And you'd have to ask these people directly, do you wish you would have just

00:06:17,420 --> 00:06:24,060
what did a mastectomy a year ago. I don't know what their answer would be. I think everybody has to

00:06:24,140 --> 00:06:34,220
feel like they tried everything before they did that. But the next question is, are such changes in

00:06:34,220 --> 00:06:46,220
a lump always bad news. I would say that if the lump is getting larger or it's moving in a direction

00:06:46,220 --> 00:06:54,300
that's growth, I would say. So I would say yes, in that sense, it's bad news. It's much, it would be

00:06:54,940 --> 00:07:03,500
worst news if it was moving towards the chest wall. So moving towards the surface is better news

00:07:03,500 --> 00:07:11,420
than a cancer moving towards the chest wall as far as the breast cancer goes. But yeah, maybe we should

00:07:11,500 --> 00:07:17,660
have a consultation about this to go into depth of everything, the changes that you're seeing.

00:07:19,260 --> 00:07:25,180
Certainly getting blood work done and it's the right thing to do to get some testing done

00:07:25,900 --> 00:07:31,900
and also getting back on the straight and narrow and different things is a good thing to do always too.

